# ZooLink MVP reverse proxy (Caddy). Terminates TLS (automatic Let's Encrypt), proxies the API,
# serves the SPA build, sets security headers. Only this service is public (ADR-0009).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Edge client-IP contract (AUDIT5 §F1b, security co-sign У-1). The API rate-limiter keys its buckets
# on X-Real-IP (backend/src/lib/rate-limit/client-ip.ts) — so this file is HALF of that control and
# the two halves are locked together by scripts/check-edge-client-ip.sh in CI (У-6).
#
#   «мы берём заголовок, который Caddy НЕ санирует (в отличие от XFF, перезаписываемого по
#   умолчанию); край обязан его перезаписать; забывчивость сделана безопасной через site-level strip
#   + CI-замок»
#
# EN: Caddy overwrites XFF by default but knows nothing about X-Real-IP — an inbound client X-Real-IP
# reaches the upstream VERBATIM (verified live against caddy:2-alpine, 2026-08-07). So:
#   (a) every handle that proxies to `api` imports the (api_upstream) snippet below, which REWRITES
#       X-Real-IP with {remote_host} — the actual TCP peer, which a client cannot forge. No `+`/`-`
#       prefix on header_up = replace, not append.
#   (b) the site-level `request_header -X-Real-IP` strips any inbound client value for ALL routes
#       BEFORE `handle` runs (directive order is Caddy's, not the file's — verified live). A future
#       handle that FORGETS the snippet therefore delivers NO header, and the API falls back to the
#       socket address (one shared bucket = today's behaviour) instead of trusting a forged value.
#       Without (b) that same forgotten handle passes `X-Real-IP: 6.6.6.6` straight through.
#
# {remote_host} is the direct peer, so this is independent of `trusted_proxies` — which is
# deliberately NOT configured here (У-2): Caddy is the only public entry point. If another proxy is
# ever placed IN FRONT of Caddy, {remote_host} becomes that proxy and this contract must be revisited.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(api_upstream) {
	reverse_proxy api:3000 {
		header_up X-Real-IP {remote_host}
	}
}

{$PUBLIC_DOMAIN} {
	encode gzip zstd

	# Security headers (security_specification.md: HSTS, etc.)
	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		X-Frame-Options "DENY"
		Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
		-Server
	}

	# Fail-safe half of the client-IP contract: no inbound X-Real-IP ever survives the edge.
	request_header -X-Real-IP

	# API
	handle /api/* {
		import api_upstream
	}

	# Health passthrough (for external uptime checks)
	handle /health/* {
		import api_upstream
	}

	# SPA static build (mounted/served separately); SPA fallback to index.html
	handle {
		root * /srv/www
		try_files {path} /index.html
		file_server
	}
}
